notes: There's a practical benefit I didn't expect. When I explain a project out loud, I wander. I double back. I remember the thing that mattered halfway through a sentence. That is not a defect to clean up; it is the talk. If the deck is built from that, the speaking comes with it. If the deck is built first, I end up writing a script that justifies an order I never chose. I would rather write the slides from the talk than the talk from the slides.
